  "unreadable": [
    "O and 0 look alike: recorded as 0 in TX0/RX0 (serial UART boxes)"
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    "Qwiic connector pin order is read from where the four leader lines (GND, 3.3V, GPIO16/SDA, GPIO17/SCL) meet the connector body; the connector's own pins are not individually drawn"
  ],
  "notes": "Callout GPIO names used as labels; white Name boxes (silkscreen) first in functions. 'CS' on GPIO21 is printed with an overline (active low). Labeled back-side pads from the insets recorded as separate connectors. Boot/Reset buttons and the WS2812 LED itself skipped."
